  "issues": [
    {
      "body": "Our Linux wayland detection looks for \"wayland-1\" but that string does not exist in that file for a standard Ubuntu 26.04 install. The system does end up detecting as having a desktop, but only because xWayland is running and our detection for x11 works on xWayland too.\n\nThat might work for some installs, but for wayland only systems, this is will likely fail.\n\nOn top of that, we do not detect mir or gamescope (the compositor of SteamOS).",
      "number": 20847,
      "title": "Linux desktop detection looks for wrong wayland string",
      "url": "https://github.com/tailscale/tailscale/issues/20847"
    }
  ],
